mesa_clc: write the SPIR-V in binary mode

On Windows "w" opens a file in text mode and every 0x0a byte of the SPIR-V
becomes 0x0d 0x0a; vtn_bindgen2 then finds a size that is not a multiple
of 4 and the libpan kernels do not build (opencl.yml, run 45763641107).

diff --git a/src/compiler/clc/mesa_clc.c b/src/compiler/clc/mesa_clc.c
index 155ea4d..8557e84 100644
--- a/src/compiler/clc/mesa_clc.c
+++ b/src/compiler/clc/mesa_clc.c
@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@ main(int argc, char **argv)
       return 1;
    }
 
-   FILE *fp = fopen(outfile, "w");
+   FILE *fp = fopen(outfile, "wb");
    fwrite(final_spirv.data, final_spirv.size, 1, fp);
    fclose(fp);
 
